cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. If you use the derived data of the evaluation, please also cite the data deposit listed under references."
title: "PlasmidCall: code and frozen models for plasmid-origin classification of short-read contigs"
abstract: >-
  Code and the frozen PlasmidCall v1.1 and v1.2-General models, which classify short-read
  assembly contigs as plasmid- or chromosome-derived from the calls of twelve published plasmid
  classifiers, with the frozen panel-output parser, a standalone scorer and its tests, and the
  design records, evidence receipts and derived tables of a prospectively sealed evaluation on
  150 bacterial genomes across six taxa. Licences: every .py, .sh and .diff file and the model files
  under models/ other than Markdown are under MIT (LICENSE); everything else, including
  documentation, tables, fixtures and metadata, is under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA).
